Z||000000||Sage||11-22-1999||01:22 PM||||Have an 88 coupe 5spd. 2.5.  SES light comes on after car is started and ran for a few minutes.  Took codes out of car shows nothing but code 23 which according to the Haynes manual is the manifold air temperature sensor code.  Problem is it is listed for v6 only.  The car came from the factory with the 4banger and as far as I know, the computer has not been changed.  Any ideas, comments or suggestions?<BR>     Got it figured out.  The 2.5 also has a manifold air temperature sensor. It is located on the top right hand side of the intake.  Book is wrong.<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 11-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||RZURCTN||11-22-1999||02:55 PM||||Are you sure that it isn't a code 32, no wait, that is v-6 only too.  I recommend that you clear the ECM by disconnecting the battery cable for 30 seconds.  Start it up and see if you get the light again.  If so, then check your code again.  Codes will stay in the computer until they are cleared.  Even if you fix the problem that gave you the code.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Sage||11-22-1999||08:57 PM||||No it was a code 23 and it was correct.  The 88 2.5 does have a manifold air temperature sensor.  I pulled out the old one and whoever put it in(it looked fairly new) either had the wrong unit, or tightened it down too much as the tip (plastic) covering the metal ends was smashed against the bottom of opening in intake!  Put new one in, problem gone...ses light out! Thanks for the input.  Oh by the way in defense of the Haynes manual, it does "mention" the m.a.t. for the 2.5 in the "revisions and updates" section for later maodels. ||||reg||1
